{
 "_notes": {
  "source": "astroloot.jar enum/constructor tables decoded with javap (build 2026-09-25). Names are the game's internal code names.",
  "fits_items_with": "boolean over the target item tags (see weapons.json tags). Engines carry the Weapon tag too, so \"!Engine && Weapon\" means a real weapon slot.",
  "level": "Mods go from level 1 to 20 (single curve astroloot.a.b.e.ax.Default, max 20).",
  "lerp(a,b)": "a + (b-a) * (lvl-1)/19, then rounded to 0.01 (to 0.001 if the result is < 0.01). Integer variant rounds to the nearest int.",
  "lerp_sq(a,b)": "a + (b-a) * ((lvl-1)/19)^2 (not rounded).",
  "lvl": "the mod level (1..20). Integer division where written, e.g. (1+(lvl/5)) = 1 + floor(lvl/5).",
  "xp_to_reach_level": "cumulative XP thresholds: threshold[i] = 250 * (2^(i+1) - 1) for i = 0..19; level = 1 + count of thresholds already reached (cap 20). So L2 needs 250, L3 750, L4 1750, L5 3750 ... L20 ~ 262,143,750? see table.",
  "drop_xp": "a dropped mod gets random starting XP: clamp(round(rand^(2+0.2*ilvl) * (PlayerXP(ilvl+8)+1)), threshold[0], threshold[last]) where PlayerXP is the player curve in player.json and rand is uniform 0..1.",
  "stat names": "class:label where label is the game text key the stat uses. Args usually start with the attribute slot (IntrinsicImplicit), then values. Percent values written as fractions (0.25 = 25%) or as whole numbers, depending on the stat (check label).",
  "unreadable": "What some unlabelled stat classes (bS, cG, ...) do exactly is not decoded; values are given raw."
 },
